# Pass B: Anima Song with Vanilla Races Expanded - Phytokin, its only optional integration.
#
# Select it with -DepMap wsl-deps.phytokin.map. The bare pass stays the default, and there is
# deliberately no wsl-deps.map beside this file: the staging script reads that name on every pass,
# so a suite owning one can never have a pass without its optional mods.
#
# Read by scripts/stage-pickle-wsl.sh: one line per mod, packageId then Workshop id.
#
# Why Phytokin is here: Anima Song looks up its sound (VRE_AnimaSongSound) and its toggle icon
# (UI/Abilities/AnimaSong) BY DEF NAME, with a Royalty fallback. The fallback that fires when it
# should not is silent by construction, and only a modlist that really contains Phytokin can show
# it. The scenario "the song and the icon follow the modlist" reads ModsConfig and demands
# Phytokin's recording and icon when the mod is active.
#
# Phytokin requires Vanilla Expanded Framework, which the staging does not pull in for an optional:
# it copies the hard dependencies of the mod under test only. VEF is listed first so it loads first.
# Biotech, which Phytokin also needs, is a DLC and is activated by the staging itself.
#
# The Workshop id was read off the item's page, https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2927323805
# on 2026-09-21, and checked on disk the same day: it declares 1.6, its packageId is the one the scenario reads,
# and its 1.6 folder defines the sound and carries the icon. The staging copies from the Windows Workshop
# folder, so Phytokin has to be subscribed there; it is, since 2026-09-21.
oskarpotocki.vanillafactionsexpanded.core   2023507013
vanillaracesexpanded.phytokin               2927323805

# The film tool again: this map REPLACES wsl-deps.map for the pass, it does not add to it, and the film scenario runs in
# this pass too.
nelim.pickletools.filmticks   path:PickleTools/FilmTicks/Mod
